# The topic manifest: the source of truth for this fork.
#
# Every change we carry lives on exactly one topic branch. The branch you
# flash -- `integration` -- is a BUILD OUTPUT, regenerated from this file by
# rebuild.sh. Never commit to integration directly; the next rebuild discards
# it, and a hunk that exists only there belongs to no PR and will be lost.
# That is not hypothetical: it is how the bridged-advert clock source came to
# sit in no branch at all for several days.
#
# Columns:  <topic branch>  <base>  [flags]
#
#   base    what the topic is rebased on. `origin/main` for an independent
#           topic; another topic when it genuinely builds on one.
#   flags   comma-separated:
#             never-upstream  local-only; never send this as a PR
#             meta            the topic tooling itself, excluded from the
#                             no-code-lost comparison in verify.sh
#
# Order matters: topics are merged top to bottom.

# --- ready to send upstream: independent, each builds on its own -----------
t/fix-packet-pool        origin/main      env=RAK_4631_repeater
t/fix-acl-flash-writes   origin/main      env=RAK_4631_repeater
# Pure tooling: one new Python file, nothing to compile.
t/tool-meshflash         origin/main

# --- the fork's tooling ----------------------------------------------------
t/meta-topics            origin/main      never-upstream,meta

# --- the feature stack, not yet carved -------------------------------------
# One topic for now, holding 64 commits across roughly ten separable areas
# (BLE bridge core, advert-set ownership, presence beacon, link reliability,
# MeshObserver, clock convergence, watchdog/boot, power estimation, bridge
# routing, docs). Carve a topic off the front of this as you prepare each PR;
# verify.sh proves the carve did not drop anything.
#
# Much of its history is intra-topic iteration -- fixes to earlier commits in
# the same stack -- which should be squashed into what it fixes before any of
# it is offered upstream. 64 commits is not 64 PRs.
t/stack                  origin/main      never-upstream,env=RAK_3401_repeater_bridge_ble
